-- THE ONE-TOKEN CONTROL for `s3-min-fully-general-sibling.mdk` (#1128).
-- Byte-identical to that file except for a single token: the general impl's head
-- reads `(Box a)` here and `a` there. Same interface, same concrete impl, same
-- data type, same three call sites, same declaration order.
--
-- SPEC ANSWER (hand-derived): `Box Int ⊏ Box a`, so
--   goal `Tag (Box Int)`    -> match {Box a, Box Int}, ⊑-minimum is Box Int => 99
--   goal `Tag (Box String)` -> match {Box a} alone                           => 10
--   goal `Tag (Box Bool)`   -> match {Box a} alone                           => 10
--
-- OBSERVED: check/run/build all ACCEPT and print 99, 10, 10. CONFORMANT.
--
-- Why this file exists: the #1128 row's comment previously named
-- `s5-argtag-unsound-under-overlap.mdk` as its "one token away" control, which an
-- adversarial review (F3) correctly rejected -- that fixture differs in the type
-- constructor, the general head AND the call-site count, so it varies three
-- things at once and isolates nothing. This file varies exactly one, which is
-- what makes #1128's trigger claim (a BARE TYPE-VARIABLE general head, not the
-- tycon and not overlap as such) an observation rather than an inference.
--
-- It also guards the fix: a change that makes #1128's row go green by breaking
-- most-specific selection for parametric heads would red THIS row instead of
-- passing silently.
data Box a = Box a

interface Tag a where
  tag : a -> Int

impl Tag (Box a) where
  tag _ = 10

impl Tag (Box Int) where
  tag _ = 99

main =
  println (tag (Box (1 : Int)))
  println (tag (Box "s"))
  println (tag (Box True))
